                <pb facs="0779" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1120 H 87/67d: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-31T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>97. Department’s No. 86, July 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d399-f1"/></p>
                <p>After consultation with Brazilian Ambassador it has been decided that the Special
                    Mission headed by the Secretary of State will proceed to Rio on the steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Pan American</hi> from New York about August 24th,
                    arriving off Rio de Janeiro about September 4th. The party will board the U. S.
                    S. <hi rendition="#italic">Maryland</hi> on the morning of September 5th and
                    enter the harbor that morning. The Commission will leave Rio de Janeiro for the
                    United States on the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">American Legion</hi> on
                    September 11th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
